    <summary>Installs Autodesk Revit 2024 without removing other Revit versions or add-ons.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Autodesk Revit is used to design, document, visualize, and deliver architecture, engineering, and construction projects.

## Why this package exists

This package installs **Revit 2024 only** and is safe to use on machines that need to keep other Revit versions. It:

- **Never uninstalls other Revit versions or Revit add-ons.** Firms routinely keep several Revit years installed because project files are locked to the version they were created in.
- **Is locked to the 2024 release line.** Upgrades only apply 2024.x versions and never jump to a later year.
- **Never force-closes Revit.** If Revit is running, the install stops with a clear message so nobody loses unsaved work. Retry when Revit is closed.
- **Respects pending reboots** instead of deleting Windows' reboot-required flag.
- **Confirms the install actually finished** by checking that Revit 2024 is registered and Revit.exe is present, with a timeout, instead of only watching for a process to exit.
- **Cleans up** the roughly 20 GB of downloaded and extracted installer files when done.
- **Checks prerequisites first** (64-bit Windows 10 version 1809 or later or Windows 11, free disk space) and fails early with a clear message.

The installer (five self-extracting parts) is downloaded from Autodesk's official distribution server and verified with a SHA-256 checksum. No Autodesk files are embedded in this package. A valid Autodesk license (named user sign-in) is required to use Revit.

## Package parameters

- `/SourcePath:` Install from a local or network folder instead of downloading from Autodesk. The folder must contain either all five official `.sfx.exe` parts (each checksum is verified) or the already extracted `setup.exe`. Example: `choco install revit2024 --params "'/SourcePath:\\nas\deploy\Revit2024'"`
- `/IgnoreRunning` Proceed even if a Revit process is running. Revit is still never closed by this package.
- `/IgnorePendingReboot` Proceed even if Windows reports a pending reboot.
- `/KeepFiles` Keep the downloaded and extracted installer files after installing.
- `/NoRestartPrompt` Don't show signed-in users the message asking them to restart when convenient. The package never restarts the computer either way.

## Notes

- Requires 64-bit Windows 10 (version 1809 or later) or Windows 11, and about 50 GB of free space on the system drive during installation.
- The download is roughly 9.6 GB in five parts. Installation typically takes 5 to 30 minutes depending on the machine and connection.
- This installs the original Revit 2024.0 release. Install later 2024 updates from Autodesk Access.
- Uninstalling this package removes Revit 2024 and the Autodesk components its installer added for 2024 (for example the 2024 Add-Ins Manager and Steel Connections content). Other Revit years, shared Autodesk components and third-party add-ons are left alone.
- After installing, signed-in users are asked to restart when convenient. Until a restart, Revit 2024 may not appear in Start menu search, and the first launch can take a minute or more.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://help.autodesk.com/view/RVT/2024/ENU/?guid=RevitReleaseNotes_2024release_html</releaseNotes>
